    "created_at": "2021-01-27T22:46:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-01-28T18:57:39Z",
    "body": "There's a similar issue with `(`, `[`, `{` etc.  The grammar spec *says* \"Note: The Other non-terminal matches any single terminal symbol except for `(`, `)`, `[`, `]`, `{`, `}` and `,`.\" but the `Other` non-terminal includes the `other` terminal, which is defined as `/[^\\t\\n\\r 0-9A-Za-z]/` and so `Other` definitely *does* match `(`, `[`, `{` etc on first glance.\r\n\r\nLike you say, this is handwaved away by the \"...one of the other terminal symbols from the grammar, it must be tokenized as the latter\" text, but it's a big footgun.",
